  "solution": {
    "text": "Here,&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;i.e. domain is <math><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and codomain is <math><mfenced open=\"(\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math><br /><br />For one-one,&nbsp;<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi> <msup> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mo>&#8242;</mo> </msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8704;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced open=\"(\" separators=\"(\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;&#160;&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is increasing in its domain. Thus, <math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is one-one in its domain.<br /><br />For onto (we find range)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;&#8658;&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;&#160;&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;&#8658;&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> as <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> <math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br />i.e., Range<math><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi></math>Codomain<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;&#160;&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is one-one but not onto.",
